  "id": "DrugBank_DB12332 - MONDO_5601",
  "verbalization": "Rucaparib, a poly(ADP-ribose) polymerase (PARP) inhibitor, is linked to Ovarian Mucinous Adenocarcinoma through a chain of indications that involve Altretamine, a chemotherapy agent. The evidence suggests that Rucaparib may exert its therapeutic effect on Ovarian Mucinous Adenocarcinoma via a mechanism that involves the indirect pathway through Altretamine. This is supported by the shared indication of Altretamine with Ovarian Mucinous Adenocarcinoma, implying a potential role for Altretamine in the pathogenesis of this cancer. The presence of multiple pathways connecting Rucaparib to Altretamine, and subsequently to Ovarian Mucinous Adenocarcinoma, suggests a possible mechanistic link involving the interaction of these entities in the context of ovarian malignancies. The integration of these pathways highlights the potential for Rucaparib to be repurposed in the treatment of Ovarian Mucinous Adenocarcinoma, particularly in cases where Altretamine is used as a therapeutic agent.",
